# Known bug: keyword counters are applied before every effect in layer 6 (layers.rs), so "loses all abilities" wipes a
# lifelink counter put on the permanent afterwards. Each counter has its own timestamp (CR 613.7c) and layer 6 applies in
# timestamp order (CR 613.7), so a counter put on after the effect gives its keyword (the Abigale, Eloquent First-Year
# ruling: "If the affected creature gains an ability after Abigale's last ability resolves, it will keep that ability").
# Oko's +1 turns Bot1's Mox Ruby into a 3/3 Elk creature that loses all abilities; afterwards Arwen's ability puts a +1/+1
# counter and a lifelink counter on it and it gains indestructible until end of turn (a later effect, so it also stays).
# Bot1 turn 1: Black Lotus (GGG), Mox Emerald, Mox Sapphire, Mox Ruby and Mox Pearl pay Arwen {1}{G}{W}, Oko {1}{G}{U}
# and Arwen's {1}.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Oko, Thief of Crowns
Arwen, Mortal Queen
Forest x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x20

